⏺ Not redundant — they answer two different questions, and tinytest correctly
  belongs in both.

  DESCRIPTION declares dependencies abstractly — what the package needs and the
  minimum acceptable version, grouped by role. Suggests: tinytest (>= 1.4.0)
  means "the test suite needs tinytest, at least 1.4.0." This is the metadata R 
  CMD check, pak, and install.packages(dependencies=TRUE) read. It is the source
  of truth for what and how new.

  renv.lock pins versions concretely — the exact installed version and its
  source, for byte-reproducible restore. tinytest 1.4.3 from RSPM records
