  file: renv/.gitignore
  status: identical
  why portable: static

  These copy between compendia as-is. One nuance: the Dockerfile is verbatim
  across fisher/peng1 only because they share the same profile, R version 
  (4.6.0), base digest, and PPM snapshot (2026-06-29). A compendium on a
  different R version or PPM date would differ in exactly those fields (FROM
  digest, RENV_CONFIG_REPOS_OVERRIDE, labels) — so "verbatim" holds within a
  profile+version cohort, not universally.

  2. Template-with-substitution — copy the template, fill per-project fields

  ┌──────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │       file       │            project-specific field            │
  ├──────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ DESCRIPTION      │ ${PKG_NAME}, ${AUTHORS_R}, license, encoding │
  ├──────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ tests/tinytest.R │ test_package("<pkgname>")                    │
  ├──────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ LICENSE          │ author + year                                │
  ├──────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ CITATION.cff     │ title, authors (peng1 only)                  │
  └──────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Same skeleton everywhere, but a handful of substituted values. These are what
  envsubst fills at scaffold; copying requires re-substituting the fields.

  3. Genuinely repo-specific — never copy

  - renv.lock — the pinned dependency closure (fisher 57, peng1 different set)
  - NAMESPACE — roxygen-generated exports for that package
  - .Rbuildignore / .gitignore — project additions (fisher adds ^archive$)
  - R/, src/, analysis/ — the actual work

  4. renv-managed / conditional — leave alone or present-when-needed

  - renv/activate.R — 1452-line diff = different renv versions; renv writes
  this, not zzcollab. Don't hand-copy; let renv manage it.
  - renv/settings.json — renv settings (fisher only)
  - .renvignore — present only when a repo has host-rendered manuscripts to
  exclude (fisher only)

  Bottom line

  The infrastructure layer (Dockerfile, Makefile, both CI workflows, .Rprofile)
  is verbatim-portable within a profile+version cohort — which is exactly why
  keeping fisher/peng1 identical was achievable and worthwhile. The identity 
  layer (DESCRIPTION/NAMESPACE/LICENSE/tinytest.R/renv.lock) is inherently
  per-project. The renv/activate.R version drift and the .Rprofile
  template-version drift are the two things currently accidentally different
